>>>Pestilence
>>I am very surprised you did Pestilence first.
>With a wand of death and plenty of blessed scrolls of charging, why not? 
>I guess maybe Famine would have been slightly safer, but I had plenty of 
>potions and a unicorn horn, which are faster to apply than eating...

That is not correct. A K-ration can be eaten in one turn and provides
nutrition for several rounds of Famine's (pathetically small) special
attack. A potion can be eaten in one turn and provides defense against
_one_ round of Pestilence's special attack. Likewise a prayer will cure
sickness once but will restore a Weak character to a state where they can
soak Famine's attack many many times. A unicorn horn is still worse, since
it takes a turn for a chance of blocking Pestilence's attack.

>The only Rider I'm really afraid of is Death, since there's no instakill.

Death can't be WoDeathed but the only thing she can do is nibble your
(almost certainly obscene) maxHP, which will take even more rounds to land
you in trouble than Famine will. However Stormbringer does not drain hit
dice from Death which might be an argument for not doing her before
Pestilence if you are very confident of your supply of sickness cures.
